1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,670
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,753 --> 00:00:08,466
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,016
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:20,061
[Ibyang] <i>I just don't want any problems</i>

7
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,062
- <i>for your family.</i>
- Ibyang?

8
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:25,400
I'm not your child.

9
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:28,153
[Ibyang] <i>I'm just borrowing you</i>
<i>as a father.</i>

10
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:33,533
[in English] Why don't you invite
Atoy over for dinner tonight?

11
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:36,161
[in English] A-Are you sure, Dad?

12
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:39,789
Maybe we'll have Daddy Atoy
here at home again.

13
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:42,751
Because he and Mommy
are getting back together!

14
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:45,462
[Red] <i>Do you remember</i>
<i>the ivory shipment before?</i>

15
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,547
<i>It failed because of him.</i>

16
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:49,174
I retaliated, and someone
got dragged into it.

17
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:50,550
What do you mean?

18
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,219
[Red] <i>I hit-and-run Atoy's father.</i>

19
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,138
[Dmitri] <i>Why are you</i>
<i>only telling me this now?</i>

20
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,265
I didn't know Atoy and Audrey
were connected.

21
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,476
[Red] <i>Our family is doomed</i>
<i>if those two end up together.</i>

22
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,311
[Atoy] <i>Good evening.</i>

23
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:06,900
Imagine, until now, I still don't know
who ran him over.

24
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,234
[in English] You wanna try it?

25
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:09,486
[Red] No need.

26
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,780
What did your father even teach you?

27
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:15,366
He was a master cutter, a tailor.

28
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,910
A gun is like a needle.

29
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:17,952
You can't tremble.

30
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:20,538
It always has to be precise.

31
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:24,417
Because the wrong hole ruins the fabric.

32
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:28,004
The wrong shot ruins the target.

33
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:30,882
And this is what I'll do to the one
who ran over my father.

34
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:32,634
‪PREVIOUSLY

35
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:34,177
[gunfire blasting]

36
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:38,348
[music fades]

37
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:40,266
Hey, wait!

38
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,769
- [Karla] What?!
- Wait, Karla!

39
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:43,978
[Billy] Are you okay?

40
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,481
You look like you're about
to explode with anger.

41
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:47,941
I really am angry!

42
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:50,276
[Billy] But wait.
We didn't do anything to you!

43
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:52,946
Wait. Are you friends with Eploks?

44
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:55,156
Do you know he's the child of a mistress?

45
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,366
No!

46
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:58,451
For me, you shouldn't judge people

47
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:01,162
because you don't know
what they're going through!

48
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:03,623
[T-Bak] Wait, wait, wait, Karla!

49
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:04,749
You!

50
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,167
Maybe you have a crush on Eploks,

51
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:08,753
that's why you're defending him
like that, huh?!

52
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:11,339
Don't you know his breath stinks?!
He has bad breath!

53
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:13,800
I don't like him!

54
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:15,552
What are you saying?!

55
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,470
It's just that Fatty is being annoying.

56
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,055
[T-Bak] I'm just saying.

57
00:02:19,889 --> 00:02:21,099
I'm out of here!

58
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:24,144
[in English] My friend!

59
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:26,729
You get irritated so easily.

60
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:29,232
- [sneaky music playing]
- [clicks tongue]

61
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:30,191
Sir,

62
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,652
right now, really?

63
00:02:33,611 --> 00:02:36,364
Can't it be at 2300 hours instead?

64
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:43,371
[suspicious music playing]

65
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:46,875
All right, sir.

66
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:49,294
[in English] I will be there ASAP.

67
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:54,132
- [phone blips]
- [music fades]

68
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:00,847
Daddy, sleep here instead.

69
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:02,181
Let's sleep together.

70
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,934
My bed is big anyway.

71
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,020
Um, even Mommy…

72
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,230
can sleep beside us.

73
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:13,860
Janine, that's not possible.

74
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,904
Why not?

75
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:19,699
I slept at Daddy's house.

76
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,951
Child, sorry.

77
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:24,454
Daddy just needs to leave.

78
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:26,039
I…

79
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:27,916
I just need to go somewhere.

80
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:28,875
Hmm?

81
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,879
Thank you. I'll go ahead.

82
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:35,465
Mm.

83
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:39,761
[somber music playing]

84
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:41,262
Uh, sir.

85
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:46,351
Thank you for giving me the chance to be

86
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:47,685
with my family and…

87
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:50,021
also with yours.

88
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,024
[in English] I'll walk him out.

89
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:54,400
[Audrey, in English] Okay, Dad.

90
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:57,153
[in English] Um, let's go, baby girl.

91
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,780
- Take care.
- [Janine, in English] Bye, Dad.

92
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:01,199
- [in English] Good night, Dad.
- [in English] Good night.

93
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:05,286
Uh, Atoy.

94
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,748
[pensive music playing]

95
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,333
Wh-Why?

96
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:14,837
I just want to be clear with you.

97
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:18,716
Just because I treated you well

98
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:21,594
doesn't mean you're the one
I want for my daughter.

99
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:24,514
I'm not arrogant.

100
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:28,559
But I'm honest about my standards.

101
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:33,106
I'm just being nice to you because
you're the father of my grandchild,

102
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,483
and that's all.

103
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,987
Uh, what do you mean?

104
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,406
[in English] You seem like a good father.

105
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,828
[in English] But I don't want you
around my daughter,

106
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,330
much more marrying her

107
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:53,042
or building a family with her.

108
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:57,213
I don't want Audrey to think
I'm separating the two of you.

109
00:04:58,047 --> 00:05:00,091
[in English] But I know
what's best for her.

110
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:03,511
And it's not you.

111
00:05:03,594 --> 00:05:08,599
[tense music playing]

112
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,835
[music fades]

113
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:40,923
[suave theme music playing]

114
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,341
[motorcycle revving]

115
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,260
- [sewing machine whirring]
- [scratches]

116
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:46,804
[snipping]

117
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:50,141
[sewing machine clacking]

118
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:52,185
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

119
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,519
[gunshots]

120
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,813
[clicking]

121
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,899
[snipping]

122
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:06,783
[music fades]

123
00:06:08,701 --> 00:06:11,621
Sir, is this sanctioned by the government?

124
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,874
[Mercado, in English]
I can neither confirm nor deny.

125
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:15,958
[in English] Again,

126
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:19,754
you are on a need-to-know basis.

127
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:21,798
[in English] Black ops?

128
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:23,382
[clicks tongue] Don't worry.

129
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:26,177
They'll triple your pay.

130
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,679
[in English] And, uh,

131
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:33,267
your mission is just
to retrieve information.

132
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,769
[suspicious music playing]

133
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:36,521
What information?

134
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:40,441
A terrorist group known as Obsidian

135
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:43,611
is reportedly training here
in the Philippines.

136
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:49,075
[Mercado] We don't know
the exact location.

137
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:51,536
But according to our intel,

138
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:56,207
they already have eight camps
here in the Philippines,

139
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:58,334
and we need to find them.

140
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,378
All of them, sir?

141
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:04,632
Your mission is to retrieve a laptop

142
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:07,176
containing the location of the camps.

143
00:07:09,303 --> 00:07:12,807
We believe someone
is supporting this group.

144
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:15,184
That's why they're camping here.

145
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,311
We don't know who.

146
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:19,564
That's why, Atoy,

147
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,108
they need your help.

148
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:29,115
This is difficult, sir.

149
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:32,034
This is a national security matter, Atoy.

150
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,538
[in English] High-risk.

151
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:38,833
[in English] But high rewards.

152
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:40,042
[music fades]

153
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,214
[loud exhale]

154
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,258
[dramatic sting]

155
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,176
‪[inaudible]

156
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,180
[Atoy] <i>I love you and Janine.</i>

157
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:53,681
<i>I want us to be whole.</i>

158
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:56,309
[pensive music playing]

159
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:01,772
[in English] Sir, I'm sorry.

160
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,442
I already have a family now.

161
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:06,444
I don't want to risk that.

162
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:09,280
[in English] I'm sorry,
but I have to decline this mission.

163
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:14,410
[epic music playing]

164
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,208
- [clicks tongue]
- [music concludes]

165
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,460
Are you sure about your decision, Atoy?

166
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,630
Sir, my situation is different now.

167
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:28,466
With all due respect.
I already have a child.

168
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,513
My priority now is my family.

169
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:34,972
[pensive music playing]

170
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:38,184
Before, I put the country first.

171
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,479
But, sir, I'm no longer in service.

172
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,023
[inhales]

173
00:08:44,106 --> 00:08:46,025
I know… [sighs]

174
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:49,070
this mission I'm giving you is difficult.

175
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:53,324
But I hope that now

176
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:56,327
I can talk

177
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:59,997
to the soldier I used to rely on.

178
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:05,378
There must be someone else
who can do this mission, sir.

179
00:09:05,461 --> 00:09:06,879
Let them do it.

180
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,924
[in English] But you're
my best tracker, Atoy.

181
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:14,512
I know you don't want
to leave your family.

182
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:20,768
But what if those terrorists start moving?

183
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:24,522
What about the families
that will be destroyed?

184
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:28,401
The mothers, fathers, and children
who will be victimized, or worse,

185
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:31,362
killed because we didn't act immediately?

186
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:36,784
[tense music playing]

187
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:41,455
Atoy.

188
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,418
[in English] Doing this for your country

189
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:47,962
is also a service to your family.

190
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:55,886
[music fades]

191
00:09:56,762 --> 00:10:00,891
- [crickets chirping]
- [clicks tongue]

192
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,101
[in English] Thanks, Dad.

193
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,770
[smirks]

194
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:07,898
That Atoy really expects
you'll give him and Audrey your blessing.

195
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:12,695
He's an idiot to think
we'll let them be together.

196
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:16,115
[sighs]

197
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:19,660
Audrey will eventually find out
what I did.

198
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:21,996
[in English] I just hope…

199
00:10:22,079 --> 00:10:24,081
- [pensive music playing]
- [inhales]

200
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:26,959
that I won't regret my decision.

201
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:31,964
I can clearly see the joy on her face.

202
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,427
There's nothing I can do, Dad.

203
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:38,804
I didn't mean for it to happen.

204
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:41,098
You should have finished off--

205
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:47,188
You should have finished off
that Atoy long ago,

206
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:49,690
so I wouldn't be worrying now!

207
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:53,194
You keep giving me problems, Red!

208
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,528
[music fades]

209
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,155
[in English] Let me correct my mistake.

210
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:58,658
[in English] I can kill him now.

211
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:01,035
[tense music playing]

212
00:11:01,118 --> 00:11:02,078
And what?

213
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:06,248
Let my grandchild grow up
without a father?!

214
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:09,377
And don't you realize?

215
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,921
If something happens to Atoy,

216
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:16,842
we'll be the first suspects
because I kept him away from Audrey!

217
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:29,063
[in English] Let me remind you.

218
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,065
[ominous music playing]

219
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:36,278
Pray that he doesn't discover
what you did to his father.

220
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:42,660
Or better yet,
prepare yourself for that day.

221
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:46,831
[tense music playing]

222
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:57,967
[music fades]

223
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,635
What is this?

224
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,430
[Atoy] "Fortishell"?

225
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:07,268
Isn't that where we get
our hard-shell cases for our equipment?

226
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:08,811
Yes.

227
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:12,731
Their products are high-quality
and military-grade.

228
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:16,277
Where can I get one of these?

229
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,945
[suspicious music playing]

230
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,072
[Mercado] It's not commercially available.

231
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:24,368
But I know
the only office distributor here.

232
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:28,289
[tense music playing]

233
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:36,172
[wind chimes clinking]

234
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:37,590
[Atoy] 'Nang!

235
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:40,551
Oh, you're still here?

236
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:42,761
Ah.

237
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,306
I just finished an order.

238
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:46,599
I'm heading home soon.

239
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:48,726
You close up, okay?

240
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,317
How's Ibyang?

241
00:12:58,652 --> 00:12:59,987
They're fine.

242
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,282
Don't worry.

243
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:06,243
The child is just fretting about you.

244
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:09,288
You know Ibyang. She'll miss you too.

245
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:12,625
Just wait. She'll be the one
to come to you.

246
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:16,337
Ah.

247
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:20,841
How was your dinner with Audrey's family?

248
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:26,722
[pensive music playing]

249
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:40,236
Her father talked to me.

250
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:46,242
He doesn't want Audrey and me
to get back together.

251
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:49,036
What about your child?

252
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:50,663
Well,

253
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:54,416
I'll still continue being a father.
That's fine with him.

254
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,210
[melancholic music playing]

255
00:13:56,293 --> 00:13:57,962
But when it comes to Audrey…

256
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:00,422
He really doesn't want it.

257
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,509
He doesn't want us to be together.

258
00:14:04,134 --> 00:14:04,969
[Cita] Oh?

259
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:07,721
Didn't Audrey object?

260
00:14:07,805 --> 00:14:09,515
[Atoy] She doesn't know, Godmother.

261
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:11,600
She doesn't know yet.

262
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,770
[heavy sigh]

263
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,484
I don't know how to tell her.

264
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:30,244
Don't worry.

265
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:33,247
Whether you and Audrey
end up together or not,

266
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:37,293
Karla and I are here as your family.

267
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:45,718
You know, honestly,
I feel uneasy about Audrey's family.

268
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:52,433
Hmm. Didn't you say Red is a bad person?

269
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:54,101
It's like he's seething inside.

270
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,853
So, maybe

271
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,938
he's just like his father?

272
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:03,736
[suspicious music playing]

273
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:15,456
[Mercado on the phone]
<i>Padua, have you left</i>

274
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:16,957
<i>the Fortishell office?</i>

275
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,084
Yes, sir. Uh, sorry.
I just got to reply now.

276
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,295
The signal inside was weak.

277
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,005
Did you get my message?

278
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:27,509
I'll send you now
the screenshot of the unit itself,

279
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:29,720
the receipt, and the order number.

280
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,598
[in English] Sir, it's confirmed.

281
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:36,060
[in English] The laptop unit was sold to

282
00:15:36,143 --> 00:15:39,021
and is registered
under the Zahran Embassy.

283
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:40,105
[Mercado, in English] <i>Good job, Atoy.</i>

284
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:46,236
I agree it's possible the laptop we're
looking for is at the Zahran Embassy.

285
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:51,367
[in English] That's why I immediately
ordered a hack on their system.

286
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:54,495
[Mercado] <i>The IT team checked the emails,</i>

287
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:58,123
<i>and the ambassador has scheduled events.</i>

288
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,667
One of which

289
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:05,506
is a meeting with expat businessmen here.

290
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,091
[in English] Copy, sir.

291
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,175
[music fades]

292
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:09,677
I know what to do.

293
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,596
[Mercado, in English]
<i>I will send you some files</i>

294
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,516
<i>of the attendees of that meeting.</i>

295
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:18,060
[tense music plays, stops]

296
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:23,941
[in English] Hey, Atoy! What's up, man?

297
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:26,068
Oh!

298
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:28,988
It seems like you're thinking
about some deep stuff, huh?

299
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,740
[in English] Is, uh, everything okay?

300
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:35,160
Oh.

301
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,745
Seems not, huh?

302
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:37,997
[in English] How can I help you?

303
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,540
[in English] Anything at all.

304
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,834
[in English] Anything?

305
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:43,085
[in English] Anything.

306
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:50,718
[sneaky music playing]

307
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,344
Are you sure, anything?

308
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,431
All right, game.

309
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:57,182
You really want to help me?

310
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:58,308
[in English] Anything.

311
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,768
[music fades]

312
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:02,271
[in English] Sir Atoy.
I'm gonna do my best.

313
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:04,690
Because I don't want you
to fail your mission.

314
00:17:05,357 --> 00:17:07,234
Thanks. Wait. Take off your towel.

315
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:09,278
- Ah, yes. Okay, okay.
- Our measurement isn't accurate.

316
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:11,321
- [sighs]
- There.

317
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:13,866
Actually, I'm kind of excited.

318
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:16,952
But, you know, also nervous.

319
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,621
But kind of just right. It's like, uh,

320
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:21,957
maybe 10% nervous and…

321
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,667
90% excited.

322
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,044
No. No, no, no.
That's wrong, that's wrong.

323
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:26,962
It's like, reversed. It's…

324
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:30,549
90% nervous and then 10% excited.

325
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:32,426
[in English] It's-- No, no, no.
That's no-- It's not right.

326
00:17:32,509 --> 00:17:33,886
It's like-- I can't explain.

327
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:36,055
[in English] It's, um… Uh…

328
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:37,639
- Oh! Can--
- There, lower your hand.

329
00:17:37,723 --> 00:17:39,141
Can I vlog this?

330
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:40,684
[music fades]

331
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:42,686
[in English] Of course not. No, of course.

332
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,897
[in English] It's-- It's a secret mission,
Brother Kurt, come on!

333
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,774
Sorry. That's a stupid question.

334
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,108
[sharp exhale]

335
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,401
[sneaky music playing]

336
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:52,154
Okay. What you need to do is simple.

337
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,073
Don't worry.

338
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:56,283
Just listen to my instructions.

339
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:57,951
- Yes.
- [in English] It will be fine.

340
00:17:58,035 --> 00:18:00,496
- [in English] Okay. Yes.
- Okay? But…

341
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:03,415
it would help more

342
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:07,252
if you knew some Russian words
or Russian phrases.

343
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:08,837
- Ah, Russian?
- Yes, Russian.

344
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,089
- [in English] Russian?
- Mm-hmm.

345
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,758
Oh-- Russian, uh-- Not really.

346
00:18:12,841 --> 00:18:14,635
[in English] I-I know a little Ilocano.

347
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:17,221
[in English] And then, uh,
I'm very good at American English,

348
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:18,180
of course, but…

349
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:20,891
I'll-- I'll learn.
I'll learn. I'll research, so…

350
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,518
so I won't embarrass myself with you.

351
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:24,478
- [in English] Research, huh? I like that.
- Yes.

352
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:25,938
- [in English] Initiative.
- [in English] Yes.

353
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:27,106
God bless.

354
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,149
- Ah. I love you.
- [chuckles]

355
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,359
[phone vibrating]

356
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,735
- [in English] Excuse me.
- [huffs] Okay.

357
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:35,364
[phone vibrating]

358
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:37,491
[in English] Hello, sir!

359
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:41,787
[clicks tongue, in English]
Doing good, sir.

360
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,413
[soft rock music playing]

361
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,667
[Atoy] <i>I found my brother…</i>

362
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:49,628
<i>Andrei Sokolov.</i>

363
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:04,476
I know your skills
aren't limited to tracking, Atoy.

364
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:08,355
You know a lot about gadgets and guns.

365
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:13,527
[Mercado] <i>But the most impressive of all…</i>
<i>You're like a chameleon.</i>

366
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,904
[in English] <i>You can be anyone.</i>

367
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,949
<i>That's why I trust you so much, Atoy.</i>

368
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:20,450
[Atoy, in English] <i>I will do my best, sir.</i>

369
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,077
[music fades]

370
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:28,792
[rock music playing]

371
00:19:37,801 --> 00:19:39,344
[music fades]

372
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,680
[Mercado on the phone]
<i>You don't just copy appearances.</i>

373
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:46,018
<i>Even the personalities</i>
<i>and characteristics,</i>

374
00:19:46,101 --> 00:19:47,352
<i>you capture them.</i>

375
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:50,314
<i>That's why you're needed for this mission.</i>

376
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:52,941
[in English] <i>Good luck, Atoy.</i>

377
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:56,236
- [guard, in English] Morning, sir.
- [Kurt, in English] Good morning.

378
00:19:57,487 --> 00:19:59,990
[Mercado on the phone]
<i>Since we now have access to the computer</i>

379
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:01,283
<i>of the ambassador's secretary…</i>

380
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:02,409
[device blips]

381
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:05,162
<i>…the name of an expat</i>
<i>was added to the list,</i>

382
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,624
<i>who is in the business</i>
<i>of selling textiles, etc.</i>

383
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:10,167
[in English] How can I help you, sir?

384
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,960
[Mercado, in English]
<i>And that's you, Atoy.</i>

385
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:14,713
- [in English] <i>You will be known as…</i>
- Sokolov.

386
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,716
Mr. Alexei Sokolov.

387
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:21,511
[in English] My brother, Andrei.

388
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,513
Andrei Sokolov.

389
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:25,766
- [computer blips]
- [in English] I'm sorry, sir.

390
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:29,519
[in English] But on my list,
it shows that you declined the invitation.

391
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:32,773
[in English] Oh, right.

392
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:36,693
[in English] Right, right. Uh, but, um…

393
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:40,447
[in English] We… We changed
our mind last minute.

394
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:43,033
[in English] C-Can you check
your email again?

395
00:20:43,116 --> 00:20:44,243
[mutters]

396
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:45,619
[music fades]

397
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:47,746
[computer blipping]

398
00:20:47,829 --> 00:20:49,706
[in English] You're correct, sir.

399
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:51,917
[in English] Our apologies
for not updating our list.

400
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:54,169
[in English] No worries.

401
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,672
[in English] Here are your access cards.

402
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:59,174
[rock music playing]

403
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:03,220
[in English] Thank you.

404
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,064
[device blips]

405
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:30,247
[suspicious music playing]

406
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:46,513
[elevator dings]

407
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:53,937
[in English] Sir, your badge?

408
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,399
Sir, you don't have access here.

409
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:02,029
Ah, sorry. I thought
this was the 12th floor.

410
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:19,296
[device blipping]

411
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:31,516
[music swells]

412
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,269
[Samir, in English] Excuse me.

413
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,104
[in English] Stop!

414
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,857
[tense music playing]

415
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,650
[in English] What is your name?

416
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,195
‪[dramatic stinging]

417
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:47,491
[in English] I am, uh, Alexei Sokolov.

418
00:22:48,158 --> 00:22:49,326
[music fades]

419
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:51,578
- [in English] You. What is your name?
- [in English] Uh, Kurt--

420
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:53,330
[Atoy clears throat, then coughs]

421
00:22:53,413 --> 00:22:54,623
Teous.

422
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:56,833
[in English] Uh,
very courteous staff here.

423
00:22:56,917 --> 00:22:59,044
[Kurt, in English] I am Andrei Sokolov.

424
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:02,506
[in English] We are the Sokolov brothers.

425
00:23:03,006 --> 00:23:04,508
[in English] You are brothers?

426
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:05,509
Uh-huh.

427
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,469
- [in English] You two?
- [Atoy] Mm-hmm.

428
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:12,682
[rousing music playing]

429
00:23:13,809 --> 00:23:16,853
[electronic blipping]

430
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:21,149
[tense music playing]

431
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:24,861
[man 1, in English]
<i>You're here for the meeting?</i>

432
00:23:24,945 --> 00:23:26,446
[in English] What business are you into?

433
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:28,198
[clicks tongue, in English] Textiles.

434
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:31,785
[in English] The ambassador
will see you now. Please come with me.

435
00:23:31,868 --> 00:23:33,954
[muttering]

436
00:23:34,037 --> 00:23:36,998
Atoy, Atoy, your neck!

437
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:37,999
I know this.

438
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,210
Atoy is pretending to be pregnant.

439
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:42,129
He should have just brought me along.

440
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:44,005
I could have been his assistant there.

441
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,757
Atoy might mess up.

442
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:47,008
[Mercado, in English] <i>Oh, you found it!</i>

443
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,343
That's our target.

444
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:52,013
[Mercado] <i>If you have the chance</i>
<i>to get it now, do it.</i>

445
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:54,766
[in English] <i>But make sure</i>
<i>you won't be compromised.</i>

446
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,268
[Samir] <i>Hey!</i>

447
00:23:56,852 --> 00:23:57,853
[in English] What are you doing here?

448
00:23:57,936 --> 00:23:58,645
‪UP NEXT

449
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:00,105
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

450
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:01,106
Uh…

451
00:24:01,189 --> 00:24:04,401
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

452
00:24:04,484 --> 00:24:06,945
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

453
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:07,946
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
